From: Stained Glass OS contributors
Subject: explorer: a desktop pager on the taskbar, four desktops, and Task View opens again

A field report: after Task View had been dismissed and the desktop switched
with Win+Ctrl+arrows, the Task View button did nothing any more. tv_close
destroyed the window from inside its own WM_ACTIVATE, the destroy did not come
back to the handler that clears the handle, and vd_taskview kept "closing" a
window that was gone. The handle is now cleared before the window is
destroyed, and a dead one is forgotten.

As asked for: a new account starts with four desktops, and the bar has a
MATE-style pager -- a box per desktop, the screen's shape, the windows drawn
as outlines, the current desktop in the accent colour; click to go there, the
wheel to step, the right button for New desktop, Close and Task View. It sits
at the right of the bar, next to the notification area, with the Task View
button just left of it.

The taskbar's accent (the active button's underline, the pager) follows
Personalization's DWM AccentColor instead of a fixed purple.

Gate: test/vdpager-gate.sh (make test-vdpager); test/vdesk-gate.sh seeds a
single desktop.
